WEBVTT

00:01.700 --> 00:04.873
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.973 --> 00:08.260
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.294 --> 00:11.813
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.848 --> 00:14.816
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.851 --> 00:18.320
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.354 --> 00:21.624
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.658 --> 00:23.192
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.243 --> 00:24.577
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.611 --> 00:27.669
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.673 --> 00:37.341
Hey, Chris, what
do you got there?

00:37.375 --> 00:39.576
I made a birdhouse
at school today.

00:39.611 --> 00:40.994
Oh, looks an
awful lot like

00:41.029 --> 00:42.696
<i>the Governor's
Mansion from Benson.</i>

00:42.731 --> 00:44.398
It is.
I'm fond of the series,

00:44.432 --> 00:46.634
and I wanted the local birds
to be aware of that.

00:46.669 --> 00:48.236
Well, I'll be on the lookout
for great tits.

00:48.270 --> 00:49.504
Peter!

00:49.522 --> 00:51.089
Well, actually, Lois,
that's a species of bird

00:51.123 --> 00:53.358
that's known to frequent
domestic birdhouses.

00:53.392 --> 00:55.076
It's why I've always
wanted a birdhouse.

00:55.111 --> 00:56.151
Hey, Lois,
let's go outside

00:56.178 --> 00:57.729
and see if we can
find some great tits.

00:57.763 --> 00:59.398
'Cause there certainly
ain't any in here!

00:59.433 --> 01:01.600
Remember those two
we saw last night?

01:01.635 --> 01:03.302
One was bigger
than the other.

01:03.336 --> 01:04.920
Yeah, and-and the bigger one
had a hair

01:04.955 --> 01:06.355
sticking out
of that pointy thing.

01:06.373 --> 01:08.190
What do you call
that pointy thing, again?

01:08.225 --> 01:09.225
The beak?
Okay.

01:09.259 --> 01:10.392
Come on, Dad!

01:10.427 --> 01:12.662
<i>Maybe we can get the birds
to act out the Benson</i>

01:12.697 --> 01:15.165
where a scheduling snafu
forces the governor to decide

01:15.199 --> 01:18.602
between meeting the president
or going to Katie's school play!

01:18.636 --> 01:19.719
Yay!

01:19.754 --> 01:21.271
Scatterbrained governor.

01:22.306 --> 01:23.490
Welp, there she is.

01:23.524 --> 01:24.659
A birdhouse.

01:24.693 --> 01:26.094
I just hope whoever moves in

01:26.128 --> 01:28.262
doesn't mind the Persian birds
next door.

01:28.297 --> 01:29.831
(Persian accent):
Eh, tweet, tweet.

01:29.865 --> 01:32.183
Check out my expensive fountain.

01:32.217 --> 01:33.434
(bird chirping)

01:33.469 --> 01:35.002
Dad, look.

01:35.037 --> 01:37.606
(birds chirping)

01:37.640 --> 01:39.608
You built
a great birdhouse, son.

01:39.642 --> 01:40.909
I'm real proud of you.

01:40.944 --> 01:42.077
Thanks, Dad.

01:42.112 --> 01:43.112
(screeching)

01:44.497 --> 01:45.697
No!

01:45.732 --> 01:46.748
What just happened?!

01:46.783 --> 01:48.117
What was that thing?!

01:48.151 --> 01:50.120
I don't know. Some
kind of super bird.

01:50.154 --> 01:52.222
Or maybe an average bird
who bought a Bowflex.

01:52.256 --> 01:54.924
Well, that super bird
ruined everything!

01:54.959 --> 01:56.793
Indeed, a force to
be reckoned with,

01:56.827 --> 01:59.295
like Secretary of
Energy Steven Chu.

01:59.330 --> 02:01.431
Secretary Chu,
Ways and Means

02:01.465 --> 02:03.400
has sent over
a preliminary budget.

02:03.435 --> 02:04.852
It looks like
the Department of Energy

02:04.886 --> 02:07.087
is looking at
a four-percent budget cut.

02:07.122 --> 02:08.973
(yelling)

02:09.007 --> 02:10.341
Okay, no budget cut.

02:10.375 --> 02:12.443
No budget cut.

02:15.898 --> 02:17.499
Has anyone seen your father?

02:17.533 --> 02:18.867
It's almost 6:00.

02:18.901 --> 02:20.001
PETER:
I am here.

02:20.036 --> 02:23.238
Family, I want you to
meet my falcon, Xerxes.

02:23.272 --> 02:24.639
I'm a falconer now.

02:24.674 --> 02:25.841
And yet for Christmas,

02:25.875 --> 02:27.877
I got a wrapped
scrambled egg.

02:27.911 --> 02:29.128
(gasping)

02:29.163 --> 02:30.897
Peter, that falcon
looks pretty dangerous.

02:30.931 --> 02:32.448
Yeah, Peter, get rid
of that thing right now

02:32.482 --> 02:33.449
and eat your dinner.

02:33.483 --> 02:34.450
No!

02:34.484 --> 02:35.451
I am a falconer

02:35.485 --> 02:37.370
and I will eat
whatever Xerxes brings me.

02:37.404 --> 02:39.121
Feed master.

02:43.511 --> 02:44.678
Peter, what the hell?

02:47.815 --> 02:50.817
For Xerxes,
every meal is a pageant.

02:52.420 --> 02:53.404
Hey, Peter.

02:53.439 --> 02:54.639
Oh, falcon. Cool.

02:54.673 --> 02:55.673
Hi, falcon.

02:55.708 --> 02:57.141
Whoa, whoa, easy
there, fella.

02:57.176 --> 02:59.143
Xerxes.
His name is Xerxes.

02:59.178 --> 03:00.578
Uh, what does
Xerxes eat?

03:00.613 --> 03:02.747
Rodents.
Now if you'll excuse me...

03:02.781 --> 03:04.015
(screams)
What the hell?!

03:04.049 --> 03:05.383
Peter, make him stop!

03:05.417 --> 03:08.254
(chuckles) Hey, what do you got
going on down there, Quagmire?

03:08.288 --> 03:09.889
You got a, you got
a rodent situation?

03:09.923 --> 03:10.956
Uh, no!

03:10.991 --> 03:12.491
Well, Xerxes seems
to think there is.

03:12.525 --> 03:13.492
Get him off, Peter!

03:13.526 --> 03:14.860
Admit you got
a rodent in there.

03:14.895 --> 03:15.878
Peter!
Admit it!

03:15.929 --> 03:17.379
(gagging)

03:17.430 --> 03:19.115
Aw, you scared him
out the front.

03:19.150 --> 03:20.433
Tony, come back!

03:26.741 --> 03:29.175
Oh, what... what...

03:29.210 --> 03:30.977
What do I do?
What do I do?

03:31.012 --> 03:33.414
Well, just hope he's not
standing on your soft spot.

03:33.448 --> 03:34.615
Well, is that possible?

03:34.650 --> 03:36.170
Because that could
really mess up my...

03:36.184 --> 03:39.420
(unintelligible slurring)

03:39.454 --> 03:40.988
Mom, I need
money for lunch.

03:41.023 --> 03:42.089
Oh, God.

03:42.124 --> 03:43.224
I'm sorry, Chris.

03:43.258 --> 03:45.394
My purse has been
missing for a day now.

03:45.428 --> 03:46.728
I-I can't find
it anywhere.

03:46.763 --> 03:47.763
Not to worry, Lois.

03:47.797 --> 03:48.931
Xerxes will find it.

03:48.965 --> 03:51.199
Xerxes, find Lois's purse.

03:52.768 --> 03:54.720
(bleating)

03:54.754 --> 03:56.772
This is
your purse now.

03:56.790 --> 03:59.042
Peter, I can't carry
my money in this.

03:59.076 --> 04:00.059
(screeching)

04:00.094 --> 04:01.961
<i>(scoffs)
Yeah, her money.</i>

04:03.030 --> 04:05.431
You're gonna love the park,
Xerxes.

04:06.817 --> 04:09.420
(laughing, whooping)

04:09.454 --> 04:11.872
I think you know
what I want.

04:14.159 --> 04:15.075
This is awesome.

04:15.110 --> 04:16.944
We should have our own TV show.

04:16.995 --> 04:18.779
♪

04:50.315 --> 04:52.449
So what do you think
about a platonic shower?

04:52.483 --> 04:53.617
(doorbell rings)

04:55.053 --> 04:56.453
Are you Peter Griffin?

04:56.487 --> 04:57.421
Yes, sir, I am.

04:57.455 --> 04:58.722
I represent the man

04:58.756 --> 05:00.825
whose sidecar motorcycle
you stole yesterday.

05:00.859 --> 05:02.393
You've piqued my
interest, go on.

05:02.428 --> 05:05.830
Unfortunately for you,
that man is very, very Jewish

05:05.864 --> 05:08.066
and is suing you
for everything you've got.

05:08.100 --> 05:09.550
Including the falcon.

05:09.585 --> 05:11.302
No! Not Xerxes!

05:13.840 --> 05:15.307
You won't get away with this.

05:15.342 --> 05:17.503
Wait till American Airlines'
magazine hears about this!

05:17.510 --> 05:19.495
(dialing)

05:19.529 --> 05:21.196
Hello, American Airlines'
magazine?

05:21.231 --> 05:23.332
Have I got a scoop for you.

05:24.367 --> 05:26.186
"Falcon stolen."

05:26.220 --> 05:28.021
Ew, there's a toenail in this.

05:28.055 --> 05:29.906
Guess I'll just go back
to coughing.

05:29.940 --> 05:31.941
(coughing)

05:39.167 --> 05:40.634
Now what are we gonna do?

05:40.669 --> 05:41.902
We have no money.

05:41.937 --> 05:44.505
That's okay, Lois,
we got a wonderful family.

05:44.539 --> 05:45.639
No, we don't.

05:45.674 --> 05:47.425
There's Meg and Dummy
and Big Head.

05:47.459 --> 05:48.592
Damn it, Peter,

05:48.627 --> 05:50.261
I'm probably gonna
have to get a job.

05:50.295 --> 05:52.414
Oh, thank God. Thought I was
gonna have to go back

05:52.448 --> 05:54.349
<i>to being on
Live with Kelly and Peter.</i>

05:54.384 --> 05:57.502
So exhausting having to do
that open-mouth smile

05:57.537 --> 05:59.137
while the guest
does their bit.

05:59.172 --> 06:01.873
<i>We're here with The Good
Wife's Christine Baranski.</i>

06:01.908 --> 06:03.976
So, Christine, you've
actually won an Emmy,

06:04.011 --> 06:05.044
is that right?

06:05.079 --> 06:07.713
<i>Yes, for playing
Maryann on Cybill.</i>

06:07.748 --> 06:09.115
Ah.

06:09.149 --> 06:10.583
<i>But my character
on The Good Wife</i>

06:10.617 --> 06:13.219
is such a complete
departure from Maryann.

06:13.253 --> 06:14.687
Ah!

06:14.721 --> 06:17.124
You've also had
quite a stage career.

06:17.158 --> 06:18.826
I believe you
won a Tony Award?

06:18.860 --> 06:20.727
Well, actually,
I've won two.

06:20.762 --> 06:22.296
Ah!

06:22.330 --> 06:23.697
And one more question,
darling.

06:23.731 --> 06:24.832
Who are you?

06:29.638 --> 06:33.007
Excuse me, would you mind
taking a look at my r├йsum├й?

06:33.041 --> 06:34.859
I haven't had
an interview in a while,

06:34.894 --> 06:38.012
and I want to make sure
it's formatted correctly.

06:41.050 --> 06:42.485
Looks okay.
Good.

06:42.519 --> 06:44.870
It's not too braggy?

06:44.905 --> 06:46.906
Hi, I'm sorry,

06:46.940 --> 06:48.607
I couldn't help
but overhear you.

06:48.642 --> 06:50.609
You have an amazing
speaking voice.

06:50.660 --> 06:51.911
My name's Randy.

06:51.945 --> 06:54.180
I can get you steady work
with a voice like that.

06:54.214 --> 06:55.182
Really?

06:55.216 --> 06:56.783
Wow, thank you.

06:56.818 --> 06:58.185
This is great.

06:58.219 --> 07:00.787
Now I won't have to become
a Mary Kay saleswoman.

07:00.822 --> 07:02.556
So, what makes
these shampoos

07:02.590 --> 07:04.391
different from the ones
at the supermarket?

07:04.425 --> 07:07.295
These shampoos
have been in my car.

07:11.700 --> 07:12.700
Guess what everybody?

07:12.734 --> 07:14.869
Oh, my God!
Tampons and groceries?

07:14.903 --> 07:18.773
No-- well, yes--
but also I got discovered today.

07:18.807 --> 07:21.059
I could be one of those
famous voice-over artists

07:21.094 --> 07:23.378
you hear on TV or in the movies.

07:23.413 --> 07:24.813
Ugh, her doing voice-over?

07:24.848 --> 07:26.215
Who wants to hear that?

07:26.249 --> 07:28.400
Maybe she could be one
of those annoying voices

07:28.434 --> 07:30.986
that goes, "Ah, ah, ah,
not that product."

07:31.020 --> 07:33.256
<i>NARRATOR: Which of these
leading brands of canned soup</i>

07:33.290 --> 07:35.458
<i>has less than
a hundred grams of sodium?</i>

07:35.493 --> 07:37.460
<i>Ah, ah, ah.Keep going.</i>

07:37.495 --> 07:38.795
<i>Not that one.</i>

07:38.829 --> 07:39.929
<i>Ah, ah, ah.</i>

07:39.964 --> 07:41.331
<i>Not that one either.</i>

07:41.365 --> 07:42.499
<i>Ah, ah, ah.</i>

07:42.533 --> 07:43.766
<i>Nope, not that one.</i>

07:43.801 --> 07:45.436
Look, this isn't even for me.

07:45.470 --> 07:47.004
It's for my homosexual lover.

07:47.038 --> 07:48.272
<i>Ah, ah, ah.</i>

07:48.306 --> 07:49.874
<i>The Bible's pretty clear
about that.</i>

07:52.944 --> 07:55.029
Hi, I'm Lois Griffin.

07:55.063 --> 07:57.014
I have an appointment
to see Randy.

07:57.065 --> 07:59.851
Lois, I'm so glad
you decided to try this.

07:59.886 --> 08:01.720
I can't believe
I'm a celebrity now.

08:01.754 --> 08:03.154
I might hit
someone with my car

08:03.189 --> 08:04.923
on the way home
just for kicks.

08:04.957 --> 08:06.424
Well, I have a feeling

08:06.459 --> 08:08.860
you're gonna be
a big star here.

08:08.895 --> 08:10.997
(phones ringing,
men chattering)

08:11.031 --> 08:12.465
What am I wearing?

08:12.499 --> 08:14.934
(giggles)
Nothing at all, sweetheart.

08:14.968 --> 08:16.502
Wait a minute.

08:16.537 --> 08:18.638
This is a phone sex operation.

08:18.672 --> 08:20.139
I can't do this.

08:20.173 --> 08:21.908
It pays two grand
a week, sweetie.

08:21.942 --> 08:22.975
Oh, my God.

08:23.010 --> 08:24.278
With that
type of money,

08:24.312 --> 08:26.780
I could buy pots and
pans at Williams-Sonoma.

08:26.814 --> 08:28.882
This is a
very nice set.

08:28.917 --> 08:30.317
You must be a
phone whore.

08:30.351 --> 08:32.386
You bet your
sweet ass I am.

08:37.786 --> 08:39.787
(phones ringing,
women chattering)

08:41.874 --> 08:43.691
All right, Lois,
you know the drill.

08:43.726 --> 08:44.926
And whatever you do,

08:44.960 --> 08:47.111
do not mention computers
or the Internet.

08:47.146 --> 08:49.415
They cannot
know about it.

08:49.449 --> 08:50.449
(phone ringing)

08:50.483 --> 08:51.750
Oh, dear.

08:53.119 --> 08:54.620
Hello?

08:54.654 --> 08:56.689
Uh, h-hi there...

08:56.723 --> 08:57.690
(clears throat)

08:57.724 --> 08:59.058
...sexy.

08:59.092 --> 09:00.559
I can tell you're
good at this.

09:00.594 --> 09:03.263
Listen, I want to double-team
you on the phone with my son.

09:03.297 --> 09:04.497
Oh.

09:04.532 --> 09:06.266
Yeah, the family's
kind of falling apart.

09:06.300 --> 09:08.585
And I'm just, uh...

09:08.619 --> 09:10.887
just a dad trying to
keep it all together.

09:10.922 --> 09:12.055
I see.

09:12.089 --> 09:13.757
Are you into guys
in wheelchairs?

09:13.791 --> 09:14.825
Not really.

09:14.860 --> 09:16.093
Oh, that's too bad,

09:16.128 --> 09:18.996
'cause, uh, my son's
in a wheelchair.

09:23.735 --> 09:24.802
Hey, Lois.

09:24.836 --> 09:26.337
So, how was your first day
of voice-over?

09:26.371 --> 09:27.739
Eh, it was nothing.

09:27.774 --> 09:29.074
Turns out,
I'm just doing

09:29.108 --> 09:31.510
very obscure
European commercials.

09:31.544 --> 09:32.945
You know,
I have got to get myself

09:32.979 --> 09:34.313
back out there, too.

09:34.347 --> 09:36.732
I haven't performed
since I was in Stewman Group.

09:36.766 --> 09:38.767
(rhythmic drumming)

09:41.322 --> 09:43.840
MAN: I don't get it.
What is this?

09:43.874 --> 09:45.341
We don't know either.

09:48.412 --> 09:49.646
(phone ringing)

09:49.680 --> 09:51.848
Hi, my name's...

09:51.882 --> 09:53.050
Classy.

09:53.084 --> 09:55.286
What can I do for you,
hot stuff?

09:55.320 --> 09:56.887
Ooh, hi, Classy.

09:56.921 --> 09:59.290
Listen, do you have
a wallet or a purse?

09:59.324 --> 10:00.858
Uh, I have a purse.

10:00.892 --> 10:01.692
Oh.

10:01.726 --> 10:02.726
Oh, baby.

10:02.761 --> 10:04.495
I want you to
take the money out

10:04.529 --> 10:06.731
and count it
really slowly.

10:06.766 --> 10:07.732
Okay.

10:07.767 --> 10:08.733
One.

10:08.768 --> 10:10.435
Ooh, that's nice.

10:10.469 --> 10:11.569
Two.

10:11.604 --> 10:13.571
Oh. Oh, my.

10:13.606 --> 10:15.907
I'm sorry, the next bill
I have in here is a ten.

10:15.941 --> 10:16.908
Oh!

10:16.942 --> 10:17.943
Oh, I love you!

10:17.978 --> 10:19.345
All that and
everything.

10:19.379 --> 10:21.013
(phone ringing)

10:21.048 --> 10:22.848
Hi, I'm Classy.

10:22.883 --> 10:24.717
All right, let's get
this going, sweet cheeks.

10:24.751 --> 10:25.718
You got a
handkerchief?

10:25.752 --> 10:27.336
Uh, yeah.

10:27.371 --> 10:29.739
Good, ball that up and
stick it in your mouth.

10:29.773 --> 10:30.774
(mouth full):
Okay.

10:30.808 --> 10:32.008
Now, what else
you got there?

10:32.026 --> 10:33.327
You got a stapler?

10:33.361 --> 10:35.028
Uh-huh, uh, yeah.

10:35.063 --> 10:36.296
Okay, why don't
you go ahead

10:36.331 --> 10:38.065
and stick that in
your mouth, too.

10:38.099 --> 10:39.800
(choking)

10:39.834 --> 10:41.101
How about a
mouse pad?

10:41.135 --> 10:42.235
Uh-huh.

10:42.270 --> 10:43.838
Yeah, go ahead
and roll that up

10:43.872 --> 10:46.174
and stuff it
in there.

10:46.208 --> 10:47.658
Did you get a
packet from HR

10:47.693 --> 10:49.127
when you started
working there?

10:49.161 --> 10:50.461
(muffled grunting)

10:50.496 --> 10:52.030
Okay, I'll take
that as a yes.

10:52.064 --> 10:55.366
And I'm pretty certain you know
what I want you to do with it.

10:55.401 --> 10:57.052
(grunting)

10:57.087 --> 10:59.705
Okay, you think you can fit
anything else in your mouth?

10:59.739 --> 11:01.540
Mm-mm.
All right, so now let's start

11:01.574 --> 11:03.208
filling up some
other places.

11:12.036 --> 11:14.637
Peter, I've had
a long day at work,

11:14.672 --> 11:17.640
and right now, sex is the last
thing I want to think about.

11:17.675 --> 11:18.691
What the hell, Lois?

11:18.726 --> 11:20.443
You never want
to do it no more.

11:20.478 --> 11:23.848
What if I told you I'm
holding in a very big dump?

11:23.882 --> 11:26.801
Peter, can't you just
use Sock Lois tonight?

11:26.835 --> 11:30.421
No! Sock Lois doesn't feel
authentic to me anymore.

11:35.428 --> 11:37.863
Hey, Joe, how often
do you have sex with Bonnie?

11:37.897 --> 11:39.965
Well, my HMO only
pays for the equipment

11:39.999 --> 11:41.366
once a year. Why?

11:41.401 --> 11:43.702
Lois barely wants
to do it no more.

11:43.736 --> 11:45.070
I'm going crazy here.

11:45.104 --> 11:46.371
Ugh. I hear you.

11:46.407 --> 11:48.174
Hey, Quagmire, do
yourself a favor:

11:48.208 --> 11:49.642
don't get married.

11:49.676 --> 11:50.777
I wasn't gonna.

11:50.811 --> 11:52.211
Good. Don't.

11:52.246 --> 11:53.246
I wasn't.

11:53.280 --> 11:54.614
Perfect. Don't.

11:54.648 --> 11:57.383
Joe, you telling me not to
has no effect on me whatsoever.

11:57.418 --> 11:58.684
I'm not gonna get married.

11:58.719 --> 12:00.554
Great. Don't.

12:00.588 --> 12:02.773
I mean it, you guys,
this no-sex thing doesn't work.

12:02.807 --> 12:04.108
I need some kind
of outlet.

12:04.142 --> 12:06.477
You know, Peter,
I got just the thing for you.

12:06.511 --> 12:08.345
There's this new phone sex
chick I been calling,

12:08.379 --> 12:09.797
and she is amazing.

12:09.831 --> 12:12.467
Gee, I don't know.
Isn't that cheating on Lois?

12:12.501 --> 12:14.068
No, look, it's
over the phone.

12:14.103 --> 12:16.171
It's like they say:
"Phonin' ain't bonin'."

12:16.205 --> 12:18.239
Yeah. Well, I guess
I could try it.

12:18.274 --> 12:19.374
Trust me, Peter.

12:19.408 --> 12:21.142
Hey, I was right
about telling you

12:21.177 --> 12:22.944
to go see the gynecologist,
wasn't I?

12:24.564 --> 12:26.732
I'd like to see some
vaginas, please.

12:26.766 --> 12:29.168
That's what we're here for.
Come on in.

12:39.564 --> 12:42.015
(dialing)

12:42.049 --> 12:43.950
Hello there, handsome.

12:43.985 --> 12:45.452
I'm Classy.

12:45.486 --> 12:49.089
Um, hi, Classy,
I'm, uh, Peter.

12:49.123 --> 12:50.091
Peter...

12:50.125 --> 12:51.292
Night Shyamalan.

12:51.326 --> 12:53.461
They call me that
'cause I got a big twist

12:53.495 --> 12:54.862
at the end
of my thing.

12:54.897 --> 12:56.314
(whispers):
Oh, my God.

12:56.348 --> 12:57.315
(clears throat)

12:57.349 --> 12:59.851
Um... well,
hello, Peter.

12:59.885 --> 13:01.786
What can I do for you?

13:01.820 --> 13:04.323
Um, you want to see some
pictures that I drew?

13:04.357 --> 13:06.208
Um, sure.

13:06.242 --> 13:07.743
This is me
on a elephant.

13:07.777 --> 13:09.611
Wow.
That's beautiful.

13:09.646 --> 13:11.997
Did you draw that
all by yourself?

13:12.031 --> 13:12.998
Uh-huh.

13:13.032 --> 13:14.600
And this is me
on the moon.

13:14.634 --> 13:16.035
I didn't really
go there.

13:16.070 --> 13:17.537
It was just in
my imagination,

13:17.571 --> 13:18.638
so I drawed it.

13:18.672 --> 13:20.974
Wow, you're
really talented.

13:21.008 --> 13:23.643
You know, there's something
about you, Classy.

13:23.677 --> 13:25.078
Something special.

13:25.112 --> 13:27.146
Aw, that's very sweet.

13:27.181 --> 13:28.415
I like your voice.

13:28.450 --> 13:30.584
It makes me want to
hear more of your voice.

13:30.619 --> 13:32.152
Hey, you want to
see a funny comic?

13:32.187 --> 13:33.654
Sure.

13:44.767 --> 13:48.570
He's scared 'cause his friends
got killed in the pie.

13:53.777 --> 13:56.679
So, Peter,
how was your day?

13:56.713 --> 13:58.014
Eh, it was okay.

13:58.048 --> 13:59.649
Except for that
Yokohama beef bowl

13:59.683 --> 14:00.783
I tried for lunch.

14:00.817 --> 14:01.918
Not sitting so well.

14:01.952 --> 14:03.553
Just "okay"?

14:03.587 --> 14:06.290
Didn't try
anything new today?

14:06.324 --> 14:07.991
Talk to anyone
interesting?

14:08.026 --> 14:09.126
No, not really.

14:09.160 --> 14:10.994
Oh, that beef bowl
is wrecking me.

14:11.029 --> 14:12.629
My stomach feels
like that time

14:12.664 --> 14:14.331
I had explosive
diarrhea.

14:14.365 --> 14:15.716
(farts loudly)

14:18.036 --> 14:19.704
<i>PETER:
Brown house.</i>

14:22.758 --> 14:23.891
(phone ringing)

14:23.926 --> 14:24.892
Hello?

14:24.927 --> 14:26.394
Um, hi, Classy.

14:26.428 --> 14:27.595
It's Peter.

14:27.630 --> 14:29.080
Oh, hi there.

14:29.114 --> 14:30.748
(giggles) I love
when you talk.

14:30.783 --> 14:33.335
Listen, um, I've had
such a good time

14:33.370 --> 14:35.037
talking to you
these past few times

14:35.055 --> 14:37.523
that I was thinking
maybe we could meet.

14:37.557 --> 14:38.757
But you're married!

14:38.792 --> 14:40.342
You've got a wife!

14:40.377 --> 14:42.428
Yeah, but she's been giving
me the cold shoulder lately.

14:42.479 --> 14:43.759
Besides, anything
that comes out,

14:43.780 --> 14:45.165
I can always
take home to her.

14:45.199 --> 14:47.250
I don't think
this is a good idea.

14:47.285 --> 14:50.654
I mean, cheating on your wife
is a very serious thing.

14:50.688 --> 14:52.922
You don't understand,
I have to meet you.

14:52.957 --> 14:54.624
I-I know it
seems sudden,

14:54.659 --> 14:57.061
but I feel a special
connection with you.

14:57.095 --> 14:58.829
Look, you name the
place and the time,

14:58.864 --> 14:59.814
and I'll be there.

14:59.848 --> 15:01.882
(whispers):
You son of a bitch!

15:03.018 --> 15:04.018
Okay.

15:04.052 --> 15:05.603
I'll meet you.

15:05.637 --> 15:06.671
Yay, I did it!

15:06.705 --> 15:08.289
Thanks, Fairy God Peter!

15:08.323 --> 15:11.510
Peter, the power was
within you all along.

15:11.544 --> 15:14.262
Now if you'll excuse me, I'm
meeting Fairy God Quagmire

15:14.297 --> 15:16.682
and Fairy God Joe down
at the Fairy God Clam.

15:16.716 --> 15:18.967
That sounds like a gay bar.
It is a gay bar.

15:25.756 --> 15:27.490
That's right, fellas,
I'm gonna meet her.

15:27.525 --> 15:28.491
Meet who?

15:28.526 --> 15:29.876
Yeah, what are you
talking about?

15:29.910 --> 15:32.579
Oh, I-I thought we were starting
in the middle to save time.

15:32.613 --> 15:33.897
The-the phone sex lady,

15:33.931 --> 15:35.699
I'm gonna meet the phone sex
lady in person.

15:35.734 --> 15:36.967
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
wait a minute, Peter.

15:37.002 --> 15:38.135
I wouldn't do that.

15:38.153 --> 15:40.371
Hang on, Quagmire,
that's a bad idea.

15:40.405 --> 15:41.872
You never want to meet

15:41.907 --> 15:43.274
those phone sex
women in person.

15:43.308 --> 15:44.792
Yeah, I know,
that's what I said.

15:44.826 --> 15:45.793
I wouldn't do it.

15:45.827 --> 15:47.127
Good. Don't.

15:47.162 --> 15:48.883
Joe, Joe, you realize
what you're telling me

15:48.915 --> 15:51.049
not to do,
I'm already not doing!

15:51.083 --> 15:52.717
Okay, I know
you should never meet

15:52.752 --> 15:53.818
a phone sex operator.

15:53.853 --> 15:55.220
All right?
I'm not an idiot.

15:55.254 --> 15:56.922
I would never meet one
of those people, ever.

15:56.956 --> 15:58.573
Good. Don't.

15:58.608 --> 16:01.110
Guys, I have to see
if she's as special in person

16:01.144 --> 16:02.411
as she is on the phone.

16:02.446 --> 16:03.946
Besides, if I listened
to you guys,

16:03.981 --> 16:06.582
I never would've got that job
as a seat filler for fetuses.

16:06.617 --> 16:08.985
Okay, let's take a look
at your baby, shall we?

16:11.238 --> 16:12.538
Hi.

16:12.573 --> 16:14.508
He'll be right back;
he's in the bathroom.

16:17.579 --> 16:19.413
Thanks for
having me, Bonnie.

16:19.447 --> 16:21.048
I just needed
someone to talk to.

16:21.082 --> 16:22.049
Sure, Lois.

16:22.083 --> 16:23.050
What's on your mind?

16:23.084 --> 16:24.718
Well, it's kind
of a long story.

16:24.752 --> 16:25.720
You see...

16:25.754 --> 16:28.456
Eight (bleep) hours later...

16:28.490 --> 16:29.857
Oh, my God!

16:29.892 --> 16:31.593
So, as far as
Peter knows,

16:31.627 --> 16:33.194
he's about to
cheat on you?

16:33.228 --> 16:35.263
Lois, you got to
draw the line here.

16:35.297 --> 16:36.731
I know.

16:36.765 --> 16:39.134
There's a lot of crazy things
I'll let Peter get away with.

16:39.169 --> 16:40.269
I even held my tongue

16:40.303 --> 16:42.371
when he went through
that anime phase.

16:42.389 --> 16:44.990
Hey, Lois, me make drive
time to super fun Clam

16:45.025 --> 16:47.192
with noble Quagmire
and wheel-monster Joe.

16:47.227 --> 16:49.428
Go, force!

17:03.094 --> 17:04.061
Peter, what...

17:04.096 --> 17:05.346
Why are you
dressed like that?

17:05.380 --> 17:06.847
What did you do
to your hair?

17:06.882 --> 17:08.950
Business trip, Lois.
Going to Chicago City.

17:08.984 --> 17:10.584
Oh... okay.

17:10.619 --> 17:11.852
I see.

17:11.887 --> 17:13.087
And in case you're
wondering why

17:13.121 --> 17:14.956
I don't have business
charts, yes, I do.

17:16.993 --> 17:19.011
All right, I got to say
good-bye to the kids.

17:20.179 --> 17:21.229
Hey, champ.

17:21.264 --> 17:22.704
I want you to have
this pocket watch.

17:22.715 --> 17:24.132
It still works,
even though it's got

17:24.167 --> 17:25.901
a lot of Civil War
brains all over it.

17:27.170 --> 17:30.273
Meg, I want you to have
this sad-sounding fart.

17:30.307 --> 17:32.558
(farting)

17:33.978 --> 17:35.545
Chris, people are
gonna tell you

17:35.579 --> 17:37.947
that you're stupid and
that you're no good.

17:38.949 --> 17:39.949
Bye, Otis!

17:50.412 --> 17:52.129
That son of a bitch.

17:56.552 --> 17:57.919
(knocking)

17:59.672 --> 18:00.638
Hello.

18:00.673 --> 18:02.257
You're...

18:02.291 --> 18:03.658
you're beautiful.

18:03.693 --> 18:05.493
So you got to meet me.

18:05.528 --> 18:07.228
Are we gonna do
this or what?

18:07.263 --> 18:09.832
Listen, I... I got to
be honest with you.

18:09.866 --> 18:11.434
I am not, in fact,

18:11.468 --> 18:13.069
the President
of Hot Wheels.

18:13.103 --> 18:15.137
And I also lied about
the giant chef's hat.

18:15.172 --> 18:16.639
I do not have one.

18:16.673 --> 18:17.773
Mm-hmm.

18:17.808 --> 18:19.408
Well, the small
lies don't matter.

18:19.443 --> 18:20.444
Let's go.

18:22.313 --> 18:24.548
(sighs)
Why am I doing this?

18:24.582 --> 18:26.767
You know, I got the greatest
wife in the world.

18:26.801 --> 18:28.685
And we have
one beautiful child.

18:28.720 --> 18:31.188
But did you ever feel like
something was missing?

18:31.222 --> 18:33.024
You know,
something you had once,

18:33.058 --> 18:34.475
but now it's gone?

18:34.510 --> 18:37.128
You mean like the loyalty
of someone you trusted?

18:37.162 --> 18:40.098
Yes, I know exactly
what that feels like.

18:40.132 --> 18:41.999
Yeah, I mean, I was
just goofing around

18:42.017 --> 18:44.502
when I first called you,
but when I heard your voice,

18:44.520 --> 18:47.672
I-I felt like I found
some part of me that was lost.

18:47.690 --> 18:49.975
Doesn't make any sense,
but it...

18:50.009 --> 18:52.928
it felt like some force in
the universe wanted us together.

18:52.962 --> 18:55.931
That's... kind of nice.

18:55.965 --> 18:58.033
I guess I could understand that.

18:58.068 --> 18:59.969
Now that you're here
in front of me,

19:00.004 --> 19:02.772
I think you're the most
beautiful woman I've ever seen.

19:02.807 --> 19:05.125
♪

19:13.618 --> 19:16.287
Eight (bleep) hours later...

19:19.107 --> 19:23.344
Ah, I got to say,
I was fantastic.

19:23.378 --> 19:26.615
You think so, you
dirty, rotten cheater?!

19:26.649 --> 19:28.049
(gasps) Lois!

19:28.084 --> 19:29.951
You-you-you-you
is the phone lady,

19:29.986 --> 19:31.386
you the phone,
you the phone,

19:31.420 --> 19:32.854
you is the phone lady,
you is the phone lady,

19:32.889 --> 19:33.989
you is the phone lady...

19:34.023 --> 19:36.041
You cheated on me!
Lois!

19:36.075 --> 19:37.827
Why the hell were
you doing phone sex?!

19:37.861 --> 19:39.462
I was providing
for our family.

19:39.496 --> 19:40.680
You were lying.

19:40.714 --> 19:42.849
I'm starting to think
that whole Chicago City

19:42.883 --> 19:44.667
business trip was just
a bunch of baloney!

19:44.701 --> 19:45.935
That's not the point!

19:45.969 --> 19:47.436
Well, if you think
about it,

19:47.471 --> 19:49.957
I-I wasn't really cheating
'cause it was with you.

19:50.008 --> 19:51.608
Well, you didn't
know that!

19:51.643 --> 19:53.210
Yeah, but you know what?

19:53.244 --> 19:55.779
In some way, I think I did.

19:55.814 --> 19:57.648
You know, when I heard
your voice on that phone,

19:57.682 --> 19:58.916
I-I felt something.

19:58.950 --> 20:00.584
It was like an instinct,
you know?

20:00.618 --> 20:02.320
Both my heart and my wiener

20:02.354 --> 20:04.622
somehow knew
you were my soul mate.

20:04.657 --> 20:06.891
Well...

20:06.926 --> 20:09.594
I suppose you did
fall for me pretty hard.

20:09.628 --> 20:10.662
Don't you see, Lois?

20:10.696 --> 20:12.997
I fell in love with you
all over again.

20:13.032 --> 20:16.368
And, look, now we just had the
best sex in years because of it.

20:16.403 --> 20:19.538
I know. It's like our privates
were shaking hands

20:19.573 --> 20:22.174
after a successful business
meeting in a swamp.

20:22.209 --> 20:24.176
To me it... it just proves

20:24.211 --> 20:26.512
that we're truly meant
to be together.

20:26.546 --> 20:29.182
Oh, I love you, Peter.

20:29.217 --> 20:31.051
I love you, too, Lois.

20:34.589 --> 20:37.557
By the way, you may have to
become a full-on prostitute,

20:37.592 --> 20:40.061
'cause our phone bill
was $7,000.

20:43.832 --> 20:45.600
Oh, Peter.

20:45.634 --> 20:49.036
I want you to do me so hard
that we have to change churches.

20:49.071 --> 20:50.188
Gross!

20:51.107 --> 20:52.725
I want to wreck you so bad,

20:52.759 --> 20:54.376
you'll look like
an exploded Hot Pocket.

20:54.411 --> 20:55.845
Oh, my God!

20:58.700 --> 21:00.818
STEWIE: Can I interest you guys
in a two-and-a-quarter way?

21:00.819 --> 22:01.819
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru